just can't offer 'em.

291
00:13:22,335 --> 00:13:26,571
What?
Gasoline directly
to their doorsteps.

292
00:13:26,573 --> 00:13:28,139
Door-to-door gasoline
salesmen.

293
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:31,109
Oh, my God. That's amazing.
That's a brilliant
plan, right?

294
00:13:31,111 --> 00:13:33,144
Brains, looks, brains.
Whatever, fine.
Then I'll be the muscle.

295
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:35,046
I'll muscle these pricks
into buying the gas and--
Ooh.

296
00:13:35,048 --> 00:13:39,250
Actually, why don't you muscle
your way back by the van because
you look like a burned-up freak.

297
00:13:39,252 --> 00:13:41,352
You know what?
A look is gonna be
a big part of this.

298
00:13:41,354 --> 00:13:45,290
- I'm gonna get some disguises.
- Why would we need
disguises, Charlie?

299
00:13:45,292 --> 00:13:47,091
So people don't know
who we are, you know?

300
00:13:47,093 --> 00:13:51,496
- They already don't know.
- You're not letting
the wild card do his thing.

301
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:56,067
